 be different in the  books but for some reason they don't  want to show us some of the things lady  stoneheart might do  not only that but they could have  brought her back without spoiling  anything from george's books  they could have just given her character  a different ending like they have done  with so many others  they also revealed one of the biggest  secrets in the story  which was who is jon snow's real mother  and father  now maybe i'm just being selfish for  wanting to see lady stoneheart so bad  but they already revealed so much anyway  so why not just  include her too it would have made the  show even better  now let me show you the second reason  they gave the second reason was that  even when writing season 3  the duo knew they were going to do a  major death and resurrection across  seasons 5 and 6.  and they wanted to make sure that stayed  shocking and suspenseful  we knew we had jon snow's resurrection  coming up benioff says too many  resurrections start to diminish the  impact a character is dying  you know what i actually won't argue  with that because i do kind of agree  with it to some extent  now i would still rather have lady  stoneheart than not having her at all  but if you want to argue this reasoning  then feel free to sound off down in the  comments section of the video  you know i always love to hear what you  have to say now i want to show you their  third reason for not including lady  stoneheart because i do have something  to say about this  their third reason was that the red  wedding was one of the show's most  powerful moments  a dramatic home run as executed by  director david nutter  and the show's cast had exactly the  impact they had long hoped for  the share runners felt that bringing  back a former catelyn stark  might weaken what was accomplished by  the scene in that a silent  undead version of catelyn seemed beneath  the dignity of actress michelle fairley  who was already supernaturally haunting  as a doomed human 